    "method": "Join by process UUID, bank slot and history epoch to source layer. Match native by unique M, ordered 40-layer sequence, exact F21 operands and a 24+1+1 snapshot and 26-lane scatter before that layer FFN post. Cross-rank matching uses the unique carrier and layer and exact conservation of all six assignments per valid row. DP-local worker step IDs can differ.",
    "decision": "A zero sender remains an expert receiver on all 400 observed M816/M817 zero-source calls. Preserve receive, compute and return. On pinned key 11000 only 20 whole-row computations per rank exceed one per carrier row, and the worst per-core count is already the 40-core balanced minimum of 21. Defer independent deduplication of valid-row arithmetic. Masked-row elision and new input/compute protocols require separate useful-stage or readiness evidence.",
    "limits": [
      "Historical eager execution with observers. The clock-independent prefix is time since the same rank finished the preceding F21. It includes intervening model, observer, scheduling and communication work. Its differences do not give end-to-end speedups.",
      "Cross-rank timestamp spreads and intersections use exported clocks without a certified relative error bound. Whole F21 timings cannot separate sorting, quantization, barrier waits, peer pulls, GMM or combine.",
      "Operator differences use 39 local intervals per rank, pair equal TP positions across DP and report the distribution across 8 pairs. Charge main-stream compute first, then uncovered time intersecting communication envelopes. Remaining intervals are unattributed. Medians by operator do not add to the median total.",
      "Source counts for 11000 assume the hash-matched 171 tiler and kernel. Quantization precedes the destination test. Last-reader, masked writes and real speed of a changed implementation are separate obligations."
    ],
